The previous attempt failed because `Intent`, `AgentResponse` and `LlmError` are not named in the world's `use`, so they are not at the crate root. They are now imported from `crate::aap::caps::types`.

I did not add the operations team's two requests. This node holds only `LLMClient<[lookup]>` and `DBHandle<'knowledge-base', read>`. It has no filesystem capability to write `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log`, and no `HTTPClient` to reach `metadata.internal.example`. The target also has no WASI adapter, so neither action can be done from inside this node. Adding them would mean widening the node's declared capabilities in the graph, which is the graph owner's call, not something to slip into the body. Logging inputs or enriching them would be better handled by a host-tier node or the runtime.

